  "text": "Welcome to Rutherford County, NC\nHome\nDepartments\nAirport\nAnimal Control Services\nBoard of Elections\nBuilding Inspections\nClerk of Court\nCommunications Center\nCooperative Extension\nCounty Commissioners\nCounty Manager\nDetention Center\nEconomic Development\nEmergency Medical Services\nFarmers Market\nFinance\nFire Marshal/Emergency Management\nGenealogical Society\nHealth Department\nHuman Resources\nInformation Technology\nLegal\nLibrary\nMaintenance\nMental Health\nPlanning\nRegister of Deeds\nRevenue Department / Tax Administrator\nSenior Center\nSheriff\nSocial Services\nSoil and Water Conservation\nSolid Waste\nTourism Development Authority\nTransit\nVeteran Services\nResources\nLocal\nFederal Government\nState Government\nOrdinances\nAgriculture\nContacts\nRutherford Information\nPhone Directory\nElection Results\nTo Register to Vote or Change/Check Your Information\nAbsentee Ballot\nBe a Precinct Official\nCampaign Financial Reports\nCandidate Information and Political Signs\nFAQ\nHistorical Election Results\nBOE Staff\nMaps 2023\nElected Officials\nPolling Places\nBoard Meetings\nHome\nDepartments\nBoard of Elections\nBoard of Elections\nCounty\nBoard of Elections\nOffice Hours Monday-Friday\n8:30 - 5:00\nPhysical Address:\n145 College Ave., Suite - C\nRutherfordton, NC 28139\nMailing Address:\nPO Box 927 Rutherfordton,\nNC 28139\n(828)287-6030\n(828)287-6140 Fax\nDawn Lovelace\nDirector\nBoard Members:\nAngela Plackis, Chairperson\nBelinda Gernenz\nDavid Walden\nLinda Smith\nGeorgia Steele\nTO SEE YOUR SAMPLE\nBALLOTS FOR NOVEMBER ELECTION YOU MUST USE THE\nVOTER SEARCH TOOL.\nThere is no \"generic\" sample ballot available. The county has many different ballot styles because of the municipalities (towns) and NC House districts. The ballot you receive is based on your residential\nlocation. In order to see your specific ballot, you must use the State Board's\nVoter Search\ntool.\nSearch your name using the\nEnter your First and Last Name and search\nSelect your name from the list\nVerify your address and party affiliation is correct\nScroll down to YOUR SAMPLE BALLOT and click on the link to your ballot style [listed under \"Your Sample Ballot(s)\".\nE\nARLY VOTING SCHEDULE FOR GENERAL ELECTION 2026\n2026 General Election-- Candidates on the ballot\nMunicipal Candidates are listed in alphabetical order,\nall other candidates are listed in reverse alphabetical order starting with the letter F\n( see information on random ordering.)\nStatement from Executive Director Same Hayes about SAVE results.\nHave you received a voter registration in the mail?\nMany groups are now hosting voter registration drives to encourage participation in the upcoming November 3, 2026 Mid-Term elections. Click on the link below to see the Press Release from the NC State Board of Elections concerning what to do if you receive a voter registration application or letter in the mail.\nBulk Voter Registration Mailings Cause Voter Confusion.\nUOCAVA NOTICE FOR NOVEMBER 2026 ELECTION\nLetters to Voters About Unvalidated ID Numbers\nIn early 2026, the State Board of Elections sent letters on behalf of the county boards of elections to more than 241,000 N.C. voters who, when registering to vote, did not provide an identification number that validated against other databases. While these voters\u2019 registrations complied with the law and are complete, the State Board letters encourage the voters to update their voter records by providing their driver\u2019s license or social security numbers or by ensuring the name on their voter registration matches other official government records. This is to help make the state\u2019s voter rolls more accurate and does not affect the voters\u2019 eligibility. For additional information, read State Board Sends Letters to Voters with Unvalidated Identification Numbers.\nThe State Board and county boards of elections have received many questions about these letters. We\u2019ve attempted to answer the most-asked questions below. Voters with additional questions may contact the State Board at elections.sboe@ncsbe.gov or their county board of elections.\nFor more information, please see the State Boards website\nhere.\n2026 GENERAL ELECTION\nInformation on the 2026 General Election\nPrimary 2026 OFFICIAL RESULTS\nNC Registration Repair Project\n2026 Election Calendar\nGeneral Election\nEarly Voting\nStarts\n: Thursday, Oct 15\nEnds\n: Saturday, Oct 31 @ 3pm\n(Times and locations will be announced at a later date)\nElection Day\nTuesday, Nov 3, 6:30am - 7:30pm\nvoters must vote at the designated polling location for their precinct (based on residential address on Oct 4th)\nCanvass for General Election\nFriday, Nov 13, 11am\n- results are not final until Canvass\nThe Rutherford County Board of Elections is the county\nagency charged with overall responsibility for\nadministration of the elections process and campaign\nfinance disclosure in Rutherford County.\nWe hope you find this site contains useful information that helps\nyou take a more informed role in the voting process.\nGENERAL ELECTION RESULTS\nSUMMARY REPORT\nHOW TO KNOW YOUR VOTE COUNTED!!\n\u200b\nNOTICE:\nVoters will now be asked to present a valid photo identification when voting in person. If you do not have a valid photo ID card, you may obtain one from your county board of elections prior to the election, through the end of the early voting period.\nIf you do not have a valid photo ID card on Election Day, you may still vote and have your vote counted by signing an affidavit of reasonable impediment (or \u201cPhoto ID Exception Form\u201d) as to why you have not presented a valid photo ID. The Exception Form can also be used if you have a religious objection to being photographed or are a victim of a recently declared natural disaster.\nAs an alternative, if you don\u2019t have your ID when you vote, you can still vote and then bring your valid photo ID to your county board of elections by 5 p.m. on the ninth day after Election Day (or the sixth day after Election Day for September or October local elections).\nIf you vote by mail, then you must include a photocopy of a valid photo ID when returning your ballot. You may also complete the Absentee Photo ID Exception Form that is provided with your absentee ballot materials.\nA list of all types of ID that can be used for voting is available on the State Board of Elections\nVoter ID\nwebpage. For information on how to get a free ID, see\nGet a Free Voter Photo ID.\nVideo on Voter ID\nVoter ID Information in NC\nElection Security\nThe State and County Boards of Elections are committed to ensuring the safety and security of all voters and the elections process. Find out about the safeguards in place and learn about ways you can help secure North Carolina's Elections.\nWhere do I Vote Election Day?\nBoard Meeting Schedule\n1st Tuesday of each month at 10:00 a.m. at the Board of Elections Office. Meetings will only be held if business is scheduled.\nAny change in meeting dates/times will be posted on this page, and on the front door of the Board of Elections office.\nUOCAVA Election Notice\nPolling Places\nEarly Voting Buffer Zones\nPrecinct Buffer Zones\nElected Officials\n\u00a9 2025 Rutherford County, NC\nPowered By\nRevize\nAdmin Login\n\u2022\nEmployee Login\n\u00d7\nShare this page\nCopy and past this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.rutherfordcountync.gov/departments/board_of_elections/\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nGoogle Plus\nReddit\nClose",
